        en: "Cauda Draconis",
      },
    },
    about: {
      en: "The Dragon’s Tail is the Moon’s south node, the point where the Moon’s path crosses the ecliptic going south, opposite the Head. Astrologers count it unfavourable, like Saturn or Mars, and Lilly found that it made bad things worse. In Sanskrit it is Ketu. The geomantic figure Cauda Draconis carries its name.",
    },
    description: {
      en: "The South Node, Cauda Draconis ☋: the Dragon’s Tail, opposite the Head; unfavourable like Saturn and Mars, Ketu in Sanskrit, and a geomantic figure.",
